# Optional web/.env, read by npm run auth and npm run live.
# Exported shell variables take precedence. Never prefix secrets with VITE_.
# Node >=22.13. Start everything: npm run live
# Accounts only: npm run auth (and npm run dev -- --port 5175 --strictPort separately).
BETTER_AUTH_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5175

# Development automatically generates one private persistent secret in .auth/secret.
# Production requires an explicit random secret >=32 characters; generate with:
# node -e 'console.log(require("node:crypto").randomBytes(48).toString("base64url"))'
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=

# Contains private sqlite accounts/sessions/OTP hashes and the development secret.
# Default .auth is gitignored, mode 0700, denied by Vite, never a public asset.
# Use persistent private storage in production and back it up securely.
# A custom location must also be excluded from version control by its operator.
# AUTH_DATA_DIR=.auth

# Optional Google Web OAuth client. Neither is currently provisioned.
# Both values are required together. Register the EXACT callback:
# http://127.0.0.1:5175/api/auth/callback/google
# and authorized JavaScript origin http://127.0.0.1:5175.
# Google uses existing verified same-email accounts only; create an account and
# verify its email (console link in development) before using Google.
# Preview uses port 4175; change BETTER_AUTH_URL and Google callback together.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# In development, codes and verification/reset links appear ONLY in the local
# account-server console; no outbound email is sent, even when a key is present.
# Do not expose a development server publicly or share its private email logs.
# Production: NODE_ENV=production, HTTPS BETTER_AUTH_URL and explicit secret.
# Email code/reset/verification features are disabled unless ALL are configured:
# a Resend API key, valid verified sender and nonempty comma-separated allowlist.
# Production never logs codes/links and refuses recipients outside this allowlist.
# Password account creation/sign-in remain available when email is disabled.
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# EMAIL_FROM=Determine <accounts@your-verified-domain.example>
# EMAIL_ALLOWLIST=your-authorized-test-address@example.com

# OTP: existing accounts only, 6 digits, 5 minutes, hashed, one-use, 3 guesses,
# newest resend only, 3 sends/minute/address and IP. Limits persist in sqlite.
# First email proof (OTP or verification link) clears an UNVERIFIED account's old
# password and sessions for pre-hijacking protection. Use password reset to set
# a new password afterward; later sign-ins preserve already-proven credentials.

# Optional scene descriptions for BOTH SIM and HITL during npm run live.
# No keys: Describe stays explicitly OFF; simulation and hardware keep working.
# Existing hosted Describe API: provide BOTH (base URL, without /v1/describe).
# This takes precedence over local OpenRouter when both options are configured.
# The bearer is passed privately to the Python bridges, never command arguments.
# DESCRIBE_URL=https://mansfield.tail06a975.ts.net/describe
# DESCRIBE_KEY=
#
# Or use Determine's existing OpenRouter/OpenAI-model backend locally.
# With an OpenRouter key, npm run live starts Python on 127.0.0.1:8771 with a
# random per-launch bridge bearer. Provider keys go only to that server.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=openai/gpt-6-luna
# OPENROUTER_REASONING=low
# OPENROUTER_ZDR=1
# Optional server-side endpoint override, matching the existing backend:
# OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# The external service requires tailnet access and its Describe bearer.
# Browser Describe sends only rendered World JPEGs (also in HITL), not physical
# camera frames. No real people/faces are present, so these use redacted=true.
# Determine stores/logs no images or answer text; provider retention is separate.
# OpenRouter requests data_collection=deny; ZDR=1 further restricts endpoints.
# Never put keys in VITE_ variables, client code, browser storage or URLs.
